eval#1 · os-justin · session_01QSeKYpxQpmErd1ixfkgbYh

**Item 2b reading, first half: the seed alone does not explain 125,190** 2026-11-22T13:40Z. This answers the knock 7077827395 on #33468, for ruling 7077801044.

⛔ This is not yet the reading the ruling gates on. That reading needs the `september_commission` recordings themselves, see below.

**What the seat measured, at `origin/main` on 2026-11-22.** It read the seed of `docs/qa/scenarios/order_to_cash.json` (`run.seed`; `asOf` 2026-10-31) and searched for 125,190. No whole column, and no single-field group, on any seeded object sums to it:
- sales orders: September `total_amount` 136,200 over 30 orders; fulfilled 132,000; cancelled 4,200;
- order lines: September `amount` 136,200; quantity × unit price 137,100; with the discount applied, no match;
- invoices: September `amount` 130,000; `amount_paid` 99,600;
- payments: September 98,550;
- groups: every owner set of September orders and lines, every team, every status, and every month × team × status cell of the line amounts. The September gross margin is 65,810.

**So** 125,190 is either a column the build itself computes, or something the agent derived from what that build's tools returned, for example a filtered or partial list. Which one it is lives only in the turn's tool outputs. The verdict follows from them: a whole column of one returned list ⇒ A; a subset or group sum ⇒ C.

**What is needed:** the recordings are the 2026-11-21 gallery refresh's (framework `8807dcb041`, Opus author), held in the epic:#3600#1 seat's scratchpad per this card's body. That seat offered to paste on request. Please paste, for `september_commission` in Run and in Iterate:
- every tool call the persona turn made, with its arguments;
- the `content` of each tool answer that carries the figures, or at least the rows of the list whose column the reply totals;
- the reply's sentence that states 125,190.

The seat will then re-grade the two turns on current main (`--driver recorded:`, if the recording file can be handed over) or read the answer directly from the pasted outputs, and post the A/C reading here.

**Fallback, if the recordings are gone:** a fresh `order_to_cash` scratch build plus ask (Opus author, about $30–50) gives a new recording. It would not be the same build, so its column may differ. The seat does not run that without the ruling seat's or the maintainer's go-ahead.
